 These limits are approximate, so `vmagent` can underflow or overflow them by a small percentage (usually less than 1%).
 
+## Target limiter
+
+By default, `vmagent` doesn't limit the number of scrape targets a single `job_name` can have active at once,
+regardless of which [service discovery mechanism](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/)
+(or combination of mechanisms) produced these targets. This can be dangerous if the service discovery source
+(a cloud API, an orchestrator, a catalog, etc.) is misconfigured and suddenly starts returning
+an abnormally big number of targets for a job — scraping all of them at once can spike memory and CPU usage
+and degrade scraping for every other job running on the same `vmagent` instance.
+
+The limit can be enforced in the following places{{% available_from "v1.151.0" %}}:
+
+* Via `-promscrape.targetLimitPerJob` command-line flag. This limit is applied individually
+  to every `job_name` defined in the file pointed to by `-promscrape.config`.
+* Via `target_limit` config option at [scrape_config](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#scrape_configs) section.
+  The `target_limit` allows overriding the `-promscrape.targetLimitPerJob` on a per-`scrape_config` basis.
+  If `target_limit` is set to `0`, then it isn't applied to the given `scrape_config`,
+  even if the `-promscrape.targetLimitPerJob` command-line flag is set.
+
+When the number of targets discovered for a `job_name` exceeds its `target_limit`, `vmagent` keeps scraping
+only up to that number of targets for the job — the extra targets are dropped instead of crashing `vmagent`,
+rejecting the whole job, or silently scraping everything. Targets already being scraped keep running;
+newly discovered targets are dropped once the limit is reached, regardless of which service discovery
+mechanism produced them.
+
+Dropped targets are shown, together with the reason `target limit`, at the
+`/service-discovery` and `/api/v1/targets` pages, so it is easy to notice which job(s)
+are currently hitting the limit and roughly how many targets are being excluded because of it —
+the same page already shows the `(active/discovered)` counts per job for other kinds of dropped targets.
+
 See also [cardinality explorer docs](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/single-server-victoriametrics/#cardinality-explorer).
 
 ## Monitoring
